  {
   "type": "cols",
   "layout": "33-66",
   "columns": [
    [
     {
      "type": "textmedia",
      "header": "<h1> Options &amp;<br/>Accessories </h1>",
      "body": "",
      "images": [],
      "videos": [],
      "pos": "text",
      "cols": 1,
      "valign": "top",
      "ftype": "text",
      "id": "c819",
      "bg": "",
      "space": {
       "before": "default",
       "after": "default"
      }
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "type": "accordion",
      "header": "",
      "items": [
       {
        "title": "Automatic Sliding Door",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>Before the measuring process starts, the sliding door of the measuring machine can be conveniently and simply closed automatically via the software using pneumatic systems, and opened once the measuring process is complete.</p>",
          "images": [
           {
            "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/9/9/csm_option_schiebetuer_a5040531ed.webp",
            "alt": "",
            "w": 1000,
            "h": 563
           }
          ],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "below",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "textpic",
          "id": "c868",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Vibration decoupling",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>With a dead weight of approximately 650 kg and isolators, the solid vibration platform absorbs external vibration influences at the installation location. The isolators are supplied with compressed air at 6 bar.</p>",
          "images": [
           {
            "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/5/6/csm_option_schwingungsentkopplung_c7ed36a3e7.webp",
            "alt": "",
            "w": 1000,
            "h": 563
           }
          ],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "below",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "textpic",
          "id": "c870",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Scanning measuring sensor",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>For electronic tactile measurement of, for example, the flank relief on taps. Available with Probe inserts ranging from D 0.3 mm to D 2 mm.</p>",
          "images": [
           {
            "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/2/c/csm_option_taster_12e2b69c45.webp",
            "alt": "",
            "w": 1000,
            "h": 563
           }
          ],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "below",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "textpic",
          "id": "c872",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Measuring and Inspection Tools",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>For periodic on-site inspections of your measuring machine and to verify the accuracy of through-beam and reflected-light measurements, ZOLLER offers inspection tools that correspond to your machine, such as test mandrels, diameter gauges, and angle test gauges.</p>",
          "images": [
           {
            "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/9/9/csm_option_messmittel_39f8b82e8f.webp",
            "alt": "",
            "w": 1000,
            "h": 563
           }
          ],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "below",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "textpic",
          "id": "c874",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "EMERGENCY STOP\" circuit in »the cockpit«",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>Allows all motor-driven movements to be stopped simultaneously, further enhancing the high level of safety offered by Uhing drives. Voltage to the electronic components is maintained during this process, eliminating any danger of data loss.</p>",
          "images": [
           {
            "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/2/f/csm_option_cockpit_c34b7fbb02.webp",
            "alt": "",
            "w": 1000,
            "h": 563
           }
          ],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "below",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "textpic",
          "id": "c876",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Safety Package",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>Key control elements are located on the front of the measuring machine. This ensures that you always have unobstructed access to the emergency stop switch, the reset button, the membrane keypad, and the button for starting measuring processes.</p>",
          "images": [
           {
            "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/c/d/csm_option_sicherheitspaket_95153e17e4.webp",
            "alt": "",
            "w": 1000,
            "h": 563
           }
          ],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "below",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "textpic",
          "id": "c878",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Manual RFID Read/Write Station »mslz«",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>For manual writing to or reading from the code carrier on the tool holder using a handheld reader.</p>",
          "images": [
           {
            "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/a/f/csm_option_rfid_34dfe1d75c.webp",
            "alt": "",
            "w": 1000,
            "h": 563
           }
          ],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "below",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "textpic",
          "id": "c880",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "UPS unit",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>The UPS unit ensures that your computer shuts down properly in the event of power grid faults, thereby avoiding data loss. Mains voltages of 230 V~ (Europe) or 120 V~ (U.S.) are available.</p>",
          "images": [
           {
            "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/b/2/csm_option_usv_4c4cb5d571.webp",
            "alt": "",
            "w": 1000,
            "h": 563
           }
          ],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "below",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "textpic",
          "id": "c882",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       }
      ],
      "ftype": "accordion",
      "id": "c866",
      "bg": "",
      "space": {
       "before": "default",
       "after": "default"
      }
     }
